.TH DAV\-SYNC "1" "February 2024" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
.B dav\ sync
\(en Sync local file/folder to/from the remote
file/directories.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dav\ sync
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
.I path1
.I path2
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "POSITIONAL\ ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.I path1
Path to sync from (locally or remotely if
.B dav://
url is given)
.TP
.I path2
Path to sync to (locally or remotely if
.B dav://
url is given)
.SS "OPTIONAL\ ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.B \-h\fR,\ \fB\-\-help
Show a help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Files that exist in the destination but not in the source are
deleted during sync.
.SH "SEE\ ALSO"
.BR dav\-ls (1),
.BR dav\-cp (1),
.BR dav\-mv (1),
.BR dav\-rm (1),
.BR dav\-mkdir (1),
.BR dav\-run (1),
.BR dav\-cat (1),
.\" .BR dav\-sync (1),
.BR dav\-du (1)
.P
.BR dav (1)
